#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_elliptic_nome_q

#% text
# `inverse_elliptic_nome_q(q)` gives the parameter `m` whose nome is `q`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The nome of `m` is `exp(-pi*K(1 - m)/K(m))` (`elliptic_nome_q`); this function inverts it, as `theta_2(0, q)^4/theta_3(0, q)^4` (DLMF 22.2.2).

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values; `inverse_elliptic_nome_q(0)` is 0.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inverse_elliptic_nome_q(0.1)
#% output
#= 0.8024032982175758

#% cell
inverse_elliptic_nome_q(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
inverse_elliptic_nome_q(0.5)
#% output
#= 0.99998952213731

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `elliptic_nome_q` undoes it:

#% cell
elliptic_nome_q(inverse_elliptic_nome_q(0.2))
#% output
#= 0.20000000000000032

